[64.559634, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe schema is straightforward: sales should be `quantity * unit_price`. I’ll inspect product/category counts and test rankings around the Q4 date boundary \r\nbefore writing the final query.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app && .venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\r\nimport duckdb, pandas as pd\r\nproducts = pd.read_csv('products.csv')\r\norders = pd.read_csv('orders.csv', parse_dates=['order_date'])\r\nprint(products.info())\r\nprint('products rows', len(products), 'unique ids', products.product_id.nunique(), 'categories', products.category.value_counts().to_dict())\r\nprint('orders rows', len(orders), 'date range', orders.order_date.min(), orders.order_date.max())\r\nprint('orders per quarter', orders.order_date.dt.to_period('Q').value_counts().sort_index())\r\nprint('order product ids in products?', orders.product_id.isin(products.product_id).all())\r\nprint('dup product_id in products?', products.product_id.duplicated().any())\r\nprint('nulls', products.isna().sum().to_dict(), orders.isna().sum().to_dict())\r\nPY\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
