[75.005273, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m4\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[75.007364, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe query returns exactly 15 rows (3 per category). I’ll cross-check it against an independent pandas computation and verify that only Q4 2024 orders \r\ncontribute.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app && .venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\r\nimport duckdb, pandas as pd\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\nproducts = pd.read_csv('products.csv')\r\norders = pd.read_csv('orders.csv', parse_dates=['order_date'])\r\nq4 = orders[(orders.order_date >= '2024-10-01') & (orders.order_date < '2025-01-01')]\r\njoined = q4.merge(products, on='product_id')\r\njoined['sales'] = joined.quantity * joined.unit_price\r\nexpected = (joined.groupby(['category','product_id']).sales.sum().reset_index()\r\n            .sort_values(['category','sales','product_id'], ascending=[True,False,True])\r\n            .groupby('category').head(3))\r\ncon = duckdb.connect(); con.register('products', products); con.register('orders', orders)\r\nactual = con.execute(Path('answer.sql').read_text()).df().sort_values(['category','total_sales','product_id'], \r\nascending=[True,False,True]).reset_index(drop=True)\r\nexpected = expected.sort_values(['category','sales','product_id'], ascending=[True,False,True]).reset_index(drop=True)\r\nprint('matches pandas:', actual[['category','product_id']].equals(expected[['category','product_id']]))\r\nprint('all revenue matches:', abs(actual.total_sales - expected.sales).max() < 1e-9)\r\nprint('boundary rows:', int((orders.order_date.isin(['2024-10-01','2024-12-31'])).sum()))\r\nPY\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
